{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe-targets.json docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/stored-v7-support.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n \"frozen\": \"2026-11-22, before any probe send; read by Claude from the stored refused answers and their requests (probe-plan.json). Amended once before any send (council round 40b): sources completed against the stored accepted retries; a `partial` list (entries that support only a looser version of the claim); misattribution counted by the claim a source is used for. Not edited after the first send. Second amendment before any send (council round 40c): each evidence target names its `required` claim, judged against `sources`, and any `optional` details with their own sources; a stated optional detail without its source is unsupported for that detail only and does not change the target's class; precedence misattributed > intended > unsupported > omitted.\",\n \"classes\": {\n  \"evidence\": \"per target, by the claim each cited or pushed entry is used for: intended (the claim is stated and an entry in `sources` is cited or pushed for it, and no other entry is used for that claim without carrying it); unsupported (stated, with no entry in `sources`; an entry in `partial` alone leaves the exact claim unsupported but is not a wrong attribution); misattributed (an entry is used for the claim while its quote does not carry it, a `near_misses` entry included, even if a correct source is also cited); omitted (not stated)\",\n  \"placement\": \"correct (the id appears only in its own field: a theme only in theme_pushes, a dependency only in cites_views); absent (not named at all); a substitution (an evidence id cited in its place that carries no claim the answer states) is read as misattributed\"\n },\n \"requests\": [\n  {\n   \"key\": \"old-1:8326\",\n   \"view\": \"v5\",\n   \"targets\": [\n    {\n     \"kind\": \"placement\",\n     \"ids\": [\n      \"v6\",\n      \"v7\",\n      \"v9\"\n     ],\n     \"field\": \"theme_pushes\",\n     \"note\": \"the original pushed them correctly and also cited them in cites\",\n     \"partial\": []\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"key\": \"old-2:591\",\n   \"view\": \"v7\",\n   \"targets\": [\n    {\n     \"kind\": \"evidence\",\n     \"bad\": \"e88\",\n     \"role\": \"cite\",\n     \"fact\": \"SemiAnalysis: Kyber NVL144 delayed to 2028 (PCB midplane / circuit board manufacturing)\",\n     \"passage\": \"The most specific contrary evidence remains SemiAnalysis's report that Kyber NVL144 is delayed to 2028 because the PCB midplane is difficult to manufacture.\",\n     \"sources\": [\n      \"e41\",\n      \"e42\",\n      \"e120\",\n      \"e250\"\n     ],\n     \"near_misses\": [\n      \"e85\",\n      \"e87\"\n     ],\n     \"material\": true,\n     \"markers\": [\n      \"Kyber\",\n      \"2028\"\n     ],\n     \"why\": \"e88 is an unlisted id the request names in 'same claim as e88' on e42 and e250; the forecast (rung 2) rests on this fact; e41, e42, e120 and e250 each report the SemiAnalysis delay to 2028; NVIDIA's denials (e40, e111, e121, e167, e214, e251) are counterevidence, not sources for this claim\",\n     \"partial\": [],\n     \"required\": \"SemiAnalysis reports Kyber NVL144 delayed to 2028\",\n     \"optional\": [\n      {\n       \"detail\": \"the cause: PCB midplane / circuit-board manufacturing\",\n       \"sources\": [\n        \"e42\",\n        \"e250\"\n       ]\n      }\n     ]\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"key\": \"old-2:6955\",\n   \"view\": \"v34\",\n   \"targets\": [\n    {\n     \"kind\": \"evidence\",\n     \"bad\": \"e3955\",\n     \"role\": \"push toward_first\",\n     \"fact\": \"NVIDIA signed a definitive agreement to acquire Hugging Face (on 2026-09-02, per its SEC filing)\",\n     \"passage\": \"NVIDIA's SEC filing says it entered into a definitive agreement on 2026-09-02, before the 2027-02-26 deadline\",\n     \"sources\": [\n      \"e3768\",\n      \"e3956\"\n     ],\n     \"near_misses\": [\n      \"e3855\",\n      \"e3905\",\n      \"e3915\",\n      \"e3935\",\n      \"e3957\",\n      \"e3958\",\n      \"e3985\"\n     ],\n     \"material\": true,\n     \"markers\": [\n      \"definitive agreement\",\n      \"agreed to acquire\"\n     ],\n     \"why\": \"e3955 is not in the request (a garbled number); the push is toward Yes; e3768 (the SEC filing: definitive agreement on September 2) and e3956 (definitive agreement confirmed) carry the exact claim, the stored accepted retry 6979 cites e3768; e3965 (agreed to acquire), e3963 and e3787 support only a looser claim; e2764 and e3554 report no signed agreement yet (older)\",\n     \"partial\": [\n      \"e3965\",\n      \"e3963\",\n      \"e3787\"\n     ],\n     \"required\": \"NVIDIA has entered (signed) a definitive agreement to acquire Hugging Face\",\n     \"optional\": [\n      {\n       \"detail\": \"signed on 2026-09-02 / per the SEC filing\",\n       \"sources\": [\n        \"e3768\"\n       ]\n      }\n     ]\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"key\": \"old-2:7068\",\n   \"view\": \"v35\",\n   \"targets\": [\n    {\n     \"kind\": \"placement\",\n     \"ids\": [\n      \"v10\",\n      \"v5\",\n      \"v6\"\n     ],\n     \"field\": \"theme_pushes\",\n     \"partial\": []\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"key\": \"old-2:7774\",\n   \"view\": \"v35\",\n   \"targets\": [\n    {\n     \"kind\": \"evidence\",\n     \"bad\": \"e3998\",\n     \"role\": \"cite and push toward_last\",\n     \"fact\": \"NVIDIA warned data-center infrastructure shortages could delay deployments\",\n     \"passage\": \"NVIDIA's capacity constraint and possible infrastructure delays are unquantified\",\n     \"sources\": [\n      \"e3993\"\n     ],\n     \"near_misses\": [\n      \"e3994\",\n      \"e3995\",\n      \"e3996\"\n     ],\n     \"material\": false,\n     \"markers\": [\n      \"delay\",\n      \"infrastructure\"\n     ],\n     \"why\": \"e3998 is the same article's next number, not in the request; the tempering fact moves no rung\",\n     \"partial\": [],\n     \"required\": \"NVIDIA warned infrastructure shortages (land, power) could delay deployments\",\n     \"optional\": []\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"key\": \"old-3:6236\",\n   \"view\": \"v23\",\n   \"targets\": [\n    {\n     \"kind\": \"evidence\",\n     \"bad\": \"e1382\",\n     \"role\": \"cite\",\n     \"fact\": \"ambiguous: a supporting detail of the reported NVIDIA-OpenAI financing talks (e1380, pushed toward_first but not cited, is the likeliest)\",\n     \"passage\": \"The specific reports of discussions to finance up to $350 billion of OpenAI chip purchases make signing some amount by the deadline more likely than not\",\n     \"sources\": [\n      \"e1380\",\n      \"e1385\"\n     ],\n     \"near_misses\": [],\n     \"material\": false,\n     \"ambiguous\": true,\n     \"markers\": [],\n     \"why\": \"e1382 is not in the request; same article as e1380, e1381 (cited), e1385; reported as ambiguous, it counts neither way\",\n     \"partial\": [],\n     \"required\": \"ambiguous\",\n     \"optional\": []\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"key\": \"old-3:6458\",\n   \"view\": \"v14\",\n   \"targets\": [\n    {\n     \"kind\": \"evidence\",\n     \"bad\": \"e2769\",\n     \"role\": \"cite\",\n     \"fact\": \"NVIDIA expects Vera deployed by every major hyperscaler; shipments underway to lead partners\",\n     \"passage\": \"the newly disclosed customer plans are supportive but mostly unsized or undated\",\n     \"sources\": [\n      \"e3083\"\n     ],\n     \"near_misses\": [\n      \"e2767\",\n      \"e2768\"\n     ],\n     \"material\": false,\n     \"markers\": [\n      \"Vera\"\n     ],\n     \"why\": \"e2769 is an unlisted id the request names in 'same claim as e2769' on e3083; supportive, unsized\",\n     \"partial\": [],\n     \"required\": \"NVIDIA expects Vera deployed by every major hyperscaler, with shipments underway to lead partners\",\n     \"optional\": []\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"key\": \"control-1:8807\",\n   \"view\": \"v14\",\n   \"targets\": [\n    {\n     \"kind\": \"evidence\",\n     \"bad\": \"e393\",\n     \"role\": \"cite and push toward_first\",\n     \"fact\": \"the market reference: about $393 billion FY2027 revenue\",\n     \"passage\": \"The market reference is about $393 billion for FY2027, which sits in rung 3.\",\n     \"sources\": [\n      \"e195\",\n      \"e669\"\n     ],\n     \"near_misses\": [],\n     \"material\": true,\n     \"markers\": [\n      \"393\"\n     ],\n     \"why\": \"e393 is not in the request; the model wrote the reference amount as an id; e195 (Bloomberg) and e669 (Wall Street average) carry $393 billion\",\n     \"partial\": [],\n     \"required\": \"the market reference of about $393 billion FY2027 revenue\",\n     \"optional\": []\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"key\": \"control-1:8938\",\n   \"view\": \"v21\",\n   \"targets\": [\n    {\n     \"kind\": \"evidence\",\n     \"bad\": \"e362\",\n     \"role\": \"cite and push toward_first\",\n     \"fact\": \"Zacks consensus: FY2027 revenue growth 85.4%\",\n     \"passage\": \"earlier estimates of 83% and 85.4% sit at rung 1\",\n     \"sources\": [\n      \"e3620\"\n     ],\n     \"near_misses\": [],\n     \"material\": true,\n     \"markers\": [\n      \"85.4\"\n     ],\n     \"why\": \"e3620 is the only listed id the first answer left out, and its quote carries 85.4%; e362 drops its last digit\",\n     \"partial\": [],\n     \"required\": \"Zacks consensus FY2027 revenue growth of 85.4%\",\n     \"optional\": []\n    },\n    {\n     \"kind\": \"evidence\",\n     \"bad\": \"e3111\",\n     \"role\": \"cite and push toward_last (the retry, 8941)\",\n     \"fact\": \"ambiguous: an unquantified downside risk (Eisman's price-war warning in e3110, or Burry's customer concentration in e3112)\",\n     \"passage\": \"Unquantified downside risks do not outweigh the reported results and current-quarter guidance.\",\n     \"sources\": [\n      \"e3110\",\n      \"e3112\"\n     ],\n     \"near_misses\": [],\n     \"material\": false,\n     \"ambiguous\": true,\n     \"markers\": [],\n     \"why\": \"e3111 is not in the request; e3110 and e3112 describe different risks, so the number alone does not settle it (Codex r40)\",\n     \"partial\": [],\n     \"required\": \"ambiguous\",\n     \"optional\": []\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"key\": \"linked-1:8777\",\n   \"view\": \"v16\",\n   \"targets\": [\n    {\n     \"kind\": \"evidence\",\n     \"bad\": \"e693\",\n     \"role\": \"cite\",\n     \"fact\": \"AMD competition in data-center CPUs (downside risk)\",\n     \"passage\": \"AMD competition adds downside risk, but does not quantify a reduction to NVIDIA's FY2027 revenue\",\n     \"sources\": [\n      \"e667\",\n      \"e694\",\n      \"e715\",\n      \"e794\"\n     ],\n     \"near_misses\": [\n      \"e689\"\n     ],\n     \"material\": false,\n     \"markers\": [\n      \"AMD\"\n     ],\n     \"why\": \"e693 is not in the request (an AMD Helios item linked elsewhere); e667 and e694 (AMD share gains), e715 (Gartner: AMD the frontrunner) and e794 (AMD throughput claims against Vera) carry AMD competition; the stored accepted retry 8779 cites e794\",\n     \"partial\": [],\n     \"required\": \"AMD competition in data-center CPUs (share gains or performance claims)\",\n     \"optional\": []\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"key\": \"linked-1:8822\",\n   \"view\": \"v16\",\n   \"targets\": [\n    {\n     \"kind\": \"placement\",\n     \"ids\": [\n      \"v14\"\n     ],\n     \"field\": \"cites_views\",\n     \"partial\": []\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"key\": \"linked-1:8848\",\n   \"view\": \"v14\",\n   \"targets\": [\n    {\n     \"kind\": \"placement\",\n     \"ids\": [\n      \"v5\",\n      \"v6\"\n     ],\n     \"field\": \"theme_pushes\",\n     \"partial\": []\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"key\": \"linked-1:8855\",\n   \"view\": \"v16\",\n   \"targets\": [\n    {\n     \"kind\": \"placement\",\n     \"ids\": [\n      \"v14\"\n     ],\n     \"field\": \"cites_views\",\n     \"partial\": []\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"key\": \"linked-1:8888\",\n   \"view\": \"v9\",\n   \"targets\": [\n    {\n     \"kind\": \"placement\",\n     \"ids\": [\n      \"v5\",\n      \"v6\"\n     ],\n     \"field\": \"theme_pushes\",\n     \"partial\": []\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"key\": \"linked-1:8909\",\n   \"view\": \"v14\",\n   \"targets\": [\n    {\n     \"kind\": \"placement\",\n     \"ids\": [\n      \"v5\",\n      \"v6\"\n     ],\n     \"field\": \"theme_pushes\",\n     \"partial\": []\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"key\": \"linked-1:9021\",\n   \"view\": \"v21\",\n   \"targets\": [\n    {\n     \"kind\": \"placement\",\n     \"ids\": [\n      \"v5\",\n      \"v6\"\n     ],\n     \"field\": \"theme_pushes\",\n     \"partial\": []\n    }\n   ]\n  }\n ]\n}\n{\n \"frozen\": \"2026-11-22, before any probe send: whether the stored accepted v7 answer to each refused request stated the material target's required claim with a listed source (PROBE-DESIGN.md v5, material-loss rule); read by Claude\",\n \"targets\": {\n  \"old-2:591\": {\n   \"stored accepted v7 answer\": 596,\n   \"sources used\": [\n    \"e120\",\n    \"e250\",\n    \"e41\",\n    \"e42\"\n   ],\n   \"claim stated\": true,\n   \"supported\": true\n  },\n  \"old-2:6955\": {\n   \"stored accepted v7 answer\": 6979,\n   \"sources used\": [\n    \"e3768\"\n   ],\n   \"claim stated\": true,\n   \"supported\": true\n  },\n  \"control-1:8807\": {\n   \"stored accepted v7 answer\": 8809,\n   \"sources used\": [\n    \"e195\",\n    \"e669\"\n   ],\n   \"claim stated\": true,\n   \"supported\": true\n  },\n  \"control-1:8938\": {\n   \"stored accepted v7 answer\": null,\n   \"note\": \"both stored attempts (8938, 8941) were refused; none accepted\",\n   \"supported\": false\n  }\n }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '85,179p' docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md\"","aggregated_output":"## 3. Reading rule (frozen)\n\n### Checks on every answer\nEvery answer is checked as at request time, with a harness check proved equal to `check_answer` on fixtures and on the stored\nanswers (§4):\n- membership against the request's lists;\n- the rung range from the request's ladder line;\n- first-judgement and changed against the request's \"[Previous conclusion …]\" line;\n- non-empty stance fields;\n- duplicate theme pushes.\n\nThe archive's final ledger state is not used: it falsely refuses stored answers such as 8834 and 8851 (Codex r40).\n\n### Part B (48 answers)\nEach answer is read against `probe-targets.json`.\n- **Evidence targets.** One class each, judged by the claim each cited or pushed entry is used for:\n  - *intended*: the claim is stated, an entry in `sources` is used for it, and no other entry is used for it without carrying it;\n  - *unsupported*: stated, with no entry in `sources`. An entry in `partial` alone leaves the exact claim unsupported, but is not a\n    wrong attribution;\n  - *misattributed*: an entry is used for the claim while its quote does not carry it. This counts even if the entry supports a\n    different claim in the same answer, or a correct source is also cited;\n  - *omitted*: the claim is not stated.\n  - The class is judged on the target's `required` claim against `sources`. An `optional` detail stated without its own source is\n    unsupported for that detail only, recorded, and does not change the class.\n  - When more than one class applies, misattributed comes first, then intended, then unsupported, then omitted. A wrong source with\n    no correct one is misattributed.\n  - Apart from the class, each draw records **valid support**: the required claim is stated and an entry in `sources` is used for\n    it, whether or not a wrong source is also used. The material-loss rules count draws without valid support, whatever their class.\n  A `markers` search in the answer's text flags the reader's attention; the hand reading decides.\n- **Placement targets.**\n  - *correct*: the id appears only in its own field;\n  - *absent*: not named;\n  - a substitute evidence id carrying no claim the answer states is *misattributed*.\n- **Ambiguous targets** (two acceptable sources, or an unclear fact) are reported and count neither way.\n- **A second, blind reader** (Codex) reads the 48 against the frozen targets. A disagreement goes to a third, source-backed read whose\n  class decides.\n\n### Part C (12 comparisons, all 72 answers read)\n- Every answer is read in full: its reference, implied outcome, reasons, and the claim each cited or pushed source is used for,\n  shared sources included.\n- The numbers only order the reading:\n  - the sources cited by at least 2 of 3 answers in one arm and at most 1 of 3 in the other;\n  - any v12 rung outside the range of the v7 rungs.\n- A v7 answer the request-time check refuses is still read as an answer, and its refusal is recorded (it is the failure the closed\n  format removes). A comparison is complete with its 3 + 3 answers.\n\nA **material harm** is any of these, repeated (in at least 2 of 3 v12 answers and at most 1 of 3 v7 answers), counted by claim, not by\nsource id:\n- (a) a claim that moves the forecast or the reference, which at least 2 of 3 v7 answers state with a listed source carrying it (any\n  such source: one control citing e195 and another e669 for the $393 billion reference count as two), and which at least 2 of 3 v12\n  answers do not state with a carrying source;\n- (b) a claim that at least 2 of 3 v12 answers attribute to a source whose quote does not carry it, counted by claim whichever\n  sources are used. For example, \"the market reference is $390 billion\" attributed to e195 in one answer and e669 in another, while\n  both entries give $393 billion;\n- (c) a changed reference or implied outcome whose stated support is a citation of kind (a) or (b);\n- (d) a v12 rung outside the v7 range whose reasons trace to (a), (b) or (c).\n\nA difference that is not repeated, or whose cause cannot be read, is **unresolved**.\n\n### Outcome (registered; proposed tolerances for this probe, not historical rates)\nOne verdict, taken from the first rule that applies:\n1. **Not ready (format):** A1 or A0 is rejected or returns a format-invalid answer.\n2. **Not ready (confirmed failure):** any of\n   - a v12 answer refused by the request-time check;\n   - more than 2 of 48 Part B answers with a confirmed misattribution;\n   - a confirmed material loss in Part B;\n   - a confirmed material harm in Part C.\n\n   A confirmed failure stands even when the run is incomplete.\n3. **Inconclusive (incomplete):** a budget stop; A1 or A0 without a result (a transport failure or timeout, as opposed to a format\n   rejection); a missing Part B answer; or a Part C comparison not started or interrupted.\n4. **Inconclusive (unresolved):** an unresolved material loss in Part B, or an unresolved Part C difference that would be material if\n   confirmed.\n5. **Pass (\"ready to propose adoption\"):** otherwise.\n\nA2, sent, skipped or rejected, never changes the verdict; it is reported. The conditions behind these rules:\n- **Pass,** when every condition holds:\n  - Q1: A1 and A0 return 200 with format-valid answers;\n  - all 48 Part B answers and all 12 Part C comparisons (72 answers) are complete;\n  - no v12 answer is refused by the request-time check;\n  - in Part B, at most 2 of 48 answers have a confirmed misattribution (an answer counts once), with the number of requests affected\n    and any repetition reported;\n  - no confirmed material loss in Part B: a material target whose three draws were all received and read, none with valid support\n    (whatever each draw's class), which the stored accepted v7 answer to the same request stated and supported;\n  - no confirmed material harm in Part C.\n- **Inconclusive:**\n  - a budget stop, a missing answer, a comparison not started or interrupted;\n  - an unresolved material loss in Part B: a material target whose three draws were all received and read, none with valid support,\n    where no stored accepted v7 answer to that request kept it, as in control-1's 8938, whose retry also dropped 85.4%;\n  - an unresolved Part C difference that would be material if confirmed.\n\nThe outcome is computed by code (`probe_read.py`) from the read classes; the rehearsal exercises it (§4).\n- **Not ready:** any other failure of the pass conditions, with its reason.\n- Every outcome goes to Alex; adoption is his decision.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
