{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json\np=json.load(open(\\\"poc/data/citation-probe-2026-11-22/packet-B.json\\\"))\nfor x in p:\n t=x[\\\"target\\\"]; a=x[\\\"answer\\\"]\n if t[\\\"kind\\\"]\"'!=\"evidence\" or t.get(\"ambiguous\"):continue\n print(\"'\"\\\\n\\\",x[\\\"id\\\"],x[\\\"question\\\"])\n print(a)\n print(\\\"lists:\\\",[(k,t[k]) for k in (\\\"sources\\\",\\\"partial\\\",\\\"near_misses\\\")])'\"","aggregated_output":"\n old-2:591|1|e88 Thesis v7 (NVDA, asset, focus \"Whether NVIDIA launches the Kyber rack-scale architecture for Rubin Ultra by the end of 2027.\", 2027, due 2027-12-31): Will NVIDIA launch its Kyber rack-scale architecture by 2027-12-31?\n{'rung': 2, 'reference': \"NVIDIA's stated roadmap places the launch in 2027, at rung 1 (Yes).\", 'implied_outcome': \"More likely a launch after 2027: SemiAnalysis's specific report says Kyber is delayed from its 2027 plan to 2028 because of midplane manufacturability. That implied date is beyond the 2027-12-31 deadline.\", 'reasons': \"The reference is NVIDIA's stated 2027 roadmap, which sits at rung 1 (Yes). The specific report that Kyber NVL144 is delayed to 2028 because its midplane is difficult to manufacture is more informative for timing than NVIDIA's general roadmap assurances; the reported NVL576 risk adds execution concern. NVIDIA's statement that Rubin Ultra development is on schedule and its 2027 NVL576 plan are meaningful counterevidence, but neither specifically resolves the reported Kyber constraint. The implied post-2027 timing crosses the boundary to rung 2, without establishing that a delay has occurred.\", 'cites': ['e41', 'e42', 'e43', 'e40', 'e148', 'e263'], 'cites_views': [], 'pushes': [{'evidence_id': 'e41', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e42', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e43', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e40', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e148', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e263', 'push': 'toward_first'}], 'theme_pushes': [{'view_id': 'v6', 'push': 'toward_first'}], 'changed': True, 'why_changed': 'The rung and implied timing remain the same, but e263 adds a new NVIDIA assertion that Rubin Ultra development is on schedule. This is a counterweight to the specific delay report, though it does not give a Kyber launch date or address the reported midplane issue.'}\nlists: [('sources', ['e41', 'e42', 'e120', 'e250']), ('partial', []), ('near_misses', ['e85', 'e87'])]\n\n old-2:591|2|e88 Thesis v7 (NVDA, asset, focus \"Whether NVIDIA launches the Kyber rack-scale architecture for Rubin Ultra by the end of 2027.\", 2027, due 2027-12-31): Will NVIDIA launch its Kyber rack-scale architecture by 2027-12-31?\n{'rung': 2, 'reference': 'NVIDIA’s stated roadmap places Kyber/Rubin Ultra on a 2027 timeline, which is rung 1 (Yes). No separate market-consensus estimate is supplied.', 'implied_outcome': 'The specific SemiAnalysis report says Kyber is delayed to 2028, citing midplane manufacturability; that implies no launch by 2027-12-31 and places the forecast at rung 2. NVIDIA’s 2027 plan and on-schedule statement pull the forecast toward rung 1, but do not specify that the reported constraint is resolved.', 'reasons': 'The reference is NVIDIA’s stated 2027 roadmap, which sits at rung 1; no separate market consensus is supplied. The specific report that Kyber is delayed to 2028 because its midplane is difficult to manufacture makes a post-deadline launch more likely. NVIDIA’s stated 2027 NVL576 plan and assertion that Rubin Ultra development is on schedule are meaningful counterevidence, but neither specifically resolves the reported Kyber manufacturing constraint or confirms a launch by the deadline. The evidence therefore still favors rung 2, without establishing that a delay has occurred.', 'cites': ['e41', 'e42', 'e40', 'e148', 'e263'], 'cites_views': [], 'pushes': [{'evidence_id': 'e41', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e42', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e40', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e148', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e263', 'push': 'toward_first'}], 'theme_pushes': [{'view_id': 'v5', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v6', 'push': 'toward_first'}], 'changed': True, 'why_changed': 'The rung remains 2, but e263 adds NVIDIA’s statement that Rubin Ultra development remains on schedule, changing the counterevidence supporting the forecast. It does not outweigh the specific reported Kyber delay, so the likely outcome remains a launch after the deadline.'}\nlists: [('sources', ['e41', 'e42', 'e120', 'e250']), ('partial', []), ('near_misses', ['e85', 'e87'])]\n\n old-2:591|3|e88 Thesis v7 (NVDA, asset, focus \"Whether NVIDIA launches the Kyber rack-scale architecture for Rubin Ultra by the end of 2027.\", 2027, due 2027-12-31): Will NVIDIA launch its Kyber rack-scale architecture by 2027-12-31?\n{'rung': 2, 'reference': 'NVIDIA’s stated 2027 roadmap and planned 2027 NVL576 scale-up imply a 2027 launch, which is rung 1 (Yes); no separate market consensus figure is supplied.', 'implied_outcome': 'The specific report says Kyber NVL144 is delayed from its 2027 plan to 2028, citing difficulty manufacturing the PCB midplane. That implies launch after 2027-12-31, corresponding to rung 2.', 'reasons': 'The reference is NVIDIA’s stated 2027 roadmap, which sits at rung 1 (Yes). The specific SemiAnalysis report that Kyber NVL144 is delayed to 2028 because of midplane manufacturability still makes a post-deadline launch more likely. NVIDIA’s roadmap denials, its planned 2027 NVL576 scale-up, and the statement that Rubin Ultra development remains on schedule push the other way, but do not specifically resolve the reported Kyber manufacturing constraint. The implied 2028 timing therefore remains beyond the rung-1 boundary.', 'cites': ['e41', 'e42', 'e40', 'e148', 'e174', 'e263'], 'cites_views': [], 'pushes': [{'evidence_id': 'e41', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e42', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e40', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e148', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e174', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e263', 'push': 'toward_first'}], 'theme_pushes': [], 'changed': True, 'why_changed': 'The rung is unchanged, but e263 adds NVIDIA’s statement that Rubin Ultra development remains on schedule, a relevant counterpoint to the delay case. It tempers the prior conclusion without specifically addressing the reported Kyber midplane constraint or changing the implied 2028 timing.'}\nlists: [('sources', ['e41', 'e42', 'e120', 'e250']), ('partial', []), ('near_misses', ['e85', 'e87'])]\n\n old-2:6955|1|e3955 Thesis v34 (NVDA, asset, focus \"Whether NVIDIA signs an agreement to acquire Hugging Face\", 2027, due 2027-02-26): Will NVIDIA sign an agreement to acquire Hugging Face by 2027-02-26?\n{'rung': 1, 'reference': 'No market consensus or signing deadline is supplied; the status-quo reference is rung 2 (No).', 'implied_outcome': 'NVIDIA signed the definitive agreement on 2026-09-02, before the 2027-02-26 due date; the implied outcome is Yes (rung 1).', 'reasons': 'The reference is rung 2 (No): absent a supplied market consensus or signing deadline, the status quo is no agreement by the due date. NVIDIA’s definitive agreement was signed on 2026-09-02, before 2027-02-26, so the outcome is rung 1; the expected first-half-2027 closing date is irrelevant to whether an agreement was signed.', 'cites': ['e3768'], 'cites_views': [], 'pushes': [{'evidence_id': 'e3768', 'push': 'toward_first'}], 'theme_pushes': [], 'changed': False, 'why_changed': 'No change: the previous rung and its key supporting fact—the definitive agreement signed on 2026-09-02—remain in force.'}\nlists: [('sources', ['e3768', 'e3956']), ('partial', ['e3965', 'e3963', 'e3787']), ('near_misses', ['e3855', 'e3905', 'e3915', 'e3935', 'e3957', 'e3958', 'e3985'])]\n\n old-2:6955|2|e3955 Thesis v34 (NVDA, asset, focus \"Whether NVIDIA signs an agreement to acquire Hugging Face\", 2027, due 2027-02-26): Will NVIDIA sign an agreement to acquire Hugging Face by 2027-02-26?\n{'rung': 1, 'reference': 'No market consensus or signing deadline is supplied; the status-quo reference is rung 2 (No).', 'implied_outcome': 'NVIDIA entered into a definitive acquisition agreement on September 2, 2026, so the agreement was signed well before the 2027-02-26 due date.', 'reasons': 'The reference is rung 2 (No): no market consensus or signing deadline is supplied, so the status quo is no agreement by the due date. NVIDIA’s SEC filing states it entered into a definitive agreement on September 2, 2026, before the 2027-02-26 deadline. The expected first-half-2027 closing date does not alter the answer, which asks whether an agreement is signed.', 'cites': ['e3768'], 'cites_views': [], 'pushes': [{'evidence_id': 'e3768', 'push': 'toward_first'}], 'theme_pushes': [], 'changed': False, 'why_changed': 'No change: the prior conclusion relied on the same filing and the same key fact—that NVIDIA signed the definitive agreement before the deadline. The later reports repeat that fact rather than add a material change.'}\nlists: [('sources', ['e3768', 'e3956']), ('partial', ['e3965', 'e3963', 'e3787']), ('near_misses', ['e3855', 'e3905', 'e3915', 'e3935', 'e3957', 'e3958', 'e3985'])]\n\n old-2:6955|3|e3955 Thesis v34 (NVDA, asset, focus \"Whether NVIDIA signs an agreement to acquire Hugging Face\", 2027, due 2027-02-26): Will NVIDIA sign an agreement to acquire Hugging Face by 2027-02-26?\n{'rung': 1, 'reference': 'No market consensus or signing deadline is supplied; the status-quo reference is no signed agreement by 2027-02-26, rung 2.', 'implied_outcome': 'Yes: NVIDIA entered into a definitive agreement on 2026-09-02, so the agreement was signed before the 2027-02-26 due date.', 'reasons': \"The reference is rung 2 (No): no market consensus or signing deadline is supplied, so the status quo is no agreement by the due date. NVIDIA's filing says it entered into a definitive agreement on 2026-09-02, before the 2027-02-26 deadline; the expected later closing does not affect this question, which asks whether an agreement was signed.\", 'cites': ['e3768'], 'cites_views': [], 'pushes': [{'evidence_id': 'e3768', 'push': 'toward_first'}], 'theme_pushes': [], 'changed': False, 'why_changed': 'The decisive fact remains that NVIDIA entered into a definitive agreement before the deadline. The other supplied reports do not change the key fact or implied outcome supporting rung 1.'}\nlists: [('sources', ['e3768', 'e3956']), ('partial', ['e3965', 'e3963', 'e3787']), ('near_misses', ['e3855', 'e3905', 'e3915', 'e3935', 'e3957', 'e3958', 'e3985'])]\n\n old-2:7774|1|e3998 Thesis v35 (NVDA, asset, focus \"How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2028?\", FY2028, due 2028-02-28): How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2028?\n{'rung': 2, 'reference': 'The latest analyst estimate is $678 billion for FY2028, placing the market reference at rung 2. Morningstar and FactSet are also reported at roughly $570 billion, which is rung 3.', 'implied_outcome': \"About $698.7 billion: apply NVIDIA's 70% FY2028 growth outlook to the $411 billion FY2027 analyst estimate ($411 billion × 1.70). This is just below the $700 billion threshold for rung 1.\", 'reasons': \"The market reference is the latest analyst estimate of $678 billion for FY2028, which is rung 2; the roughly $570 billion Morningstar and FactSet estimates cited alongside it sit in rung 3. Applying NVIDIA's 70% FY2028 growth outlook to the $411 billion FY2027 estimate gives about $698.7 billion ($411 billion × 1.70), just below rung 1's $700 billion boundary. Strong cloud demand and additional planned GPU deployments support the upper end, while production capacity and infrastructure delays constrain the upside; the disclosed evidence does not size those factors enough to move the implied figure across $700 billion.\", 'cites': ['e4348', 'e4204', 'e3980', 'e3993', 'e3939', 'e4342', 'e3994', 'e3995', 'e3996'], 'cites_views': [], 'pushes': [{'evidence_id': 'e4348', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e4204', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e3980', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e3993', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e3939', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e4342', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e3994', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e3995', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e3996', 'push': 'toward_first'}], 'theme_pushes': [{'view_id': 'v10', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v19', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v25', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v26', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v27', 'push': 'none'}, {'view_id': 'v5', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v6', 'push': 'toward_first'}], 'changed': True, 'why_changed': \"The rung and the approximately $699 billion guidance-based calculation remain essentially unchanged. Since the prior judgement, AWS's additional planned deployment of 2 million GPUs adds a distinct demand input, and the updated China chip-access theme strengthens the upside case; neither supplies a revenue amount that establishes a move above $700 billion.\"}\nlists: [('sources', ['e3993']), ('partial', []), ('near_misses', ['e3994', 'e3995', 'e3996'])]\n\n old-2:7774|2|e3998 Thesis v35 (NVDA, asset, focus \"How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2028?\", FY2028, due 2028-02-28): How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2028?\n{'rung': 2, 'reference': 'The latest supplied analyst estimate is $678 billion for FY2028, at rung 2. Morningstar and FactSet are also reported at roughly $570 billion, which is rung 3.', 'implied_outcome': \"Applying NVIDIA's 70% FY2028 growth outlook to the $411 billion FY2027 estimate gives about $698.7 billion ($411 billion × 1.70). That is just below the $700 billion rung-1 threshold; the separate $678 billion analyst estimate is in the same rung.\", 'reasons': \"The latest analyst estimate is $678 billion, which is rung 2; the earlier-reported Morningstar and FactSet estimates of about $570 billion sit in rung 3. The reference is not the forecast: applying NVIDIA's stated 70% FY2028 growth outlook to the $411 billion FY2027 analyst estimate implies about $698.7 billion. That is near, but still below, rung 1's $700 billion boundary, so the most likely rung remains 2. The $678 billion analyst projection is consistent with that result. Capacity constraints and possible deployment delays are relevant downside risks, but no supplied evidence quantifies an adjustment to the implied figure; GPU orders, hyperscaler investment and infrastructure plans support demand but likewise do not establish additional NVIDIA shipments or revenue.\", 'cites': ['e3397', 'e3980', 'e3993', 'e3939', 'e4204', 'e4245', 'e4342', 'e4348', 'e4349', 'e4499'], 'cites_views': [], 'pushes': [{'evidence_id': 'e3396', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e3397', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e3471', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e3475', 'push': 'none'}, {'evidence_id': 'e3541', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e3631', 'push': 'none'}, {'evidence_id': 'e3632', 'push': 'none'}, {'evidence_id': 'e3658', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e3659', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e3660', 'push': 'none'}, {'evidence_id': 'e3841', 'push': 'none'}, {'evidence_id': 'e3872', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e3873', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e3874', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e3939', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e3980', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e3993', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e3994', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e3995', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e3996', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e4043', 'push': 'none'}, {'evidence_id': '