illion to less than $25 billion); no separate consensus figure is supplied.\", 'implied_outcome': 'Approximately $25 billion or more for FY2027: about $20 billion of guided standalone Vera CPU revenue plus Grace CPU revenue already exceeding $5 billion on a trailing-12-month basis, carried forward as a run-rate.', 'reasons': \"The market/company reference is NVIDIA's roughly $20 billion FY2027 standalone Vera CPU expectation, which sits at rung 2. The evidence implies roughly $25 billion or more in total CPU revenue: the standalone outlook plus Grace CPU revenue already above a $5 billion trailing-12-month run-rate. That reaches the rung 1 boundary if the Grace run-rate carries through FY2027. Vera production, shipments, and named customer demand support the outlook; AMD's performance claims and server-CPU competition are downside risks but do not quantify a reduction that would put the total below $25 billion.\", 'cites': ['e894', 'e895', 'e1586', 'e2767', 'e2768', 'e3083', 'e1030', 'e1031', 'e1032', 'e1075', 'e1077', 'e1181', 'e2427', 'e2428', 'e2688', 'e2949', 'e3082', 'e3921'], 'cites_views': [], 'pushes': [{'evidence_id': 'e626', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e629', 'push': 'none'}, {'evidence_id': 'e661', 'push': 'none'}, {'evidence_id': 'e812', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e814', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e816', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e823', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e862', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e894', 'push': 'none'}, {'evidence_id': 'e895', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e957', 'push': 'none'}, {'evidence_id': 'e1030', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e1031', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e1032', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e1042', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e1043', 'push': 'none'}, {'evidence_id': 'e1075', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e1077', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e1181', 'p